### 1. GET all books
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books
Accept: application/json

### 2. GET book by ID (existing)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/1
Accept: application/json

### 3. GET book by ID (non-existent -> 404 ProblemDetail)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/999
Accept: application/problem+json

### 4. POST create valid book (-> 201 Created + Location header)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Designing Data-Intensive Applications",
  "author": "Martin Kleppmann",
  "year": 2017,
  "genre": "TECHNICAL"
}

### 5. POST create invalid book with empty title (-> 400 Bad Request ProblemDetail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "author": "Martin Kleppmann",
  "year": 2017,
  "genre": "TECHNICAL"
}

### 6. POST create duplicate book (-> 409 Conflict ProblemDetail)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Effective Java",
  "author": "Joshua Bloch",
  "year": 2018,
  "genre": "TECHNICAL"
}

### 7. PUT update book (-> 200 OK)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/books/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Effective Java 3rd Edition",
  "author": "Joshua Bloch",
  "year": 2018,
  "genre": "TECHNICAL"
}

### 8. DELETE book (1st call -> 204 No Content)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/1

### 9. DELETE book (2nd call -> 404 Not Found ProblemDetail)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/1

### 10. Variant 2: Sorting and filtering (?sort=year,desc&genre=NOVEL)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books?sort=year,desc&genre=NOVEL
Accept: application/json

### 11. Variant 2: Invalid sort field (?sort=invalidField,desc -> 400 Bad Request ProblemDetail)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books?sort=invalidField,desc
Accept: application/problem+json

### 12. OpenAPI v3 Document
GET http://localhost:8080/v3/api-docs

### 13. Swagger UI page
GET http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html
